      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A female patient, age 4, presented with the chief complaint of severe headaches. Onset was within the past year. A neurological evaluation was conducted with negative results. Our testing revealed a moderate hyperopic refractive error, a marked lag of accommodation, and reduced stereopsis. The refractive error was corrected and a 6 week follow-up evaluation was performed. Correction of the refractive error resulted in abatement of the headache complaint, improved visual function, and improved preschool performance."},
